  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ed1100.html",
  "prefLabel": "Ed 1111.01 Placement in the Least Restrictive Environment",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ed 1111.01 Placement in the Least Restrictive Environment.\n\n(a) Each LEA shall ensure that, to the maximum extent appropriate, children with disabilities, including children in public or private providers of special education, are educated with children who do not have disabilities and that, consistent with 34 CFR 300.114, special classes, separate schooling, or other removal of children with disabilities from the regular educational environment occurs only when the nature or severity of the disability is such that education in regular classes with the use of supplementary aids and services cannot be achieved satisfactorily.\n\n(b) A child with a disability shall be admitted to regional vocational, career or technical education center programs on the basis of vocational needs as outlined in the child’s IEP and availability of space. However, the LEA shall ensure that any child who requires vocational education and/or career and technology education as part of FAPE shall receive such services as determined by the IEP team in the least restrictive environment.\n\nSource. (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Ed 1100) #9197, eff 6-28-08; ss by #12141, eff 3-24-17",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ed1100.html"
}
